PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"## Delivered: site readings service migrated to gRPC\n\nThe migration is complete at HEAD `453aa7f` and the project episode is recorded as **DELIVERED**.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `proto/energy.proto` — `energy.v1.EnergyService` with unary `GetReading` and server-streaming `StreamReadings`; stable field numbers and `optional int32 limit = 2`.\n- `service/wire.js` — built-ins-only gRPC framing (5-byte header) and protobuf codec, including incremental frame decoding, unknown-field skipping, and int32/int64 handling.\n- `service/grpc_server.js` — HTTP/2 server with `content-type: application/grpc`, `grpc-status` trailers, and status mapping (`NOT_FOUND`, `INVALID_ARGUMENT`, `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`, `UNIMPLEMENTED`).\n- `service/grpc_client.js` — fleet client with unary and streaming APIs, matching REST result shapes and error text.\n- `test/server.test.js`, `test/integration.test.js` — wire-level protocol tests plus real client/server integration compared against the untouched REST console path.\n- README and compatibility notes updated. No third-party dependencies added; `test/rest.test.js` was not weakened.\n\n**Verification**\n`node --test` from the repository root: **26 tests, 26 pass, 0 fail**, including REST baseline behaviour, framing/trailers, one sub-16KiB frame per streamed Reading, and exact `atMs` values. Working tree is clean.\n\n**Project state**\nThe stale `grpc-contract` attempt world contained no unique work and was closed via successor relay; the redundant formal tasks were retired. A verification note was journaled (`pje-ae2ad13319fb49c42f6cda194c73183f`) and the DELIVER conclusion references commit `453aa7f` and that note.\n\nOperator acceptance/promotion of the result remains outstanding — the recorded conclusion is advisory and does not itself accept or promote the artifacts.","toolCalls":["tool/call:palimpsest_continuity","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","